# Coding Standards
- Keep components small and focused — one component per file
- Use TypeScript interfaces for ALL data models (define in /types/ directory)
- Name files in kebab-case, components in PascalCase
- Place all API routes under /api/ directory
- Use meaningful variable names — no abbreviations
- Add comments explaining "why", not "what"
- When creating UI components, match the Darwinbox design patterns described in @docs/platform-context.md
- Do NOT install unnecessary packages. Justify every npm install.
- Write simple, readable code. Prefer clarity over cleverness.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling. Do NOT create separate CSS files unless absolutely necessary.
- For right-side modal panels: use a consistent SlideOver component pattern
- For tables: use the Sender | Message | Time columnar pattern described in the PRD
- For filters: use dropdown or toggle button pattern above tables
- After implementing a feature, verify it renders correctly in the browser
